<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>3.3. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1 on iOS UIKit Course</title><link>/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/</link><description>Recent content in 3.3. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1 on iOS UIKit Course</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>3.3.1. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIPickerView</title><link>/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.4.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-2-uipickerview/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.4.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-2-uipickerview/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="331-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uipickerview"&gt;3.3.1. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIPickerView&lt;a class="anchor" href="#331-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uipickerview"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src="/gitbook-assets/Screenshot 2023-05-11 at 12.13.48 PM (1).png" alt=""&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now let&amp;rsquo;s open the second screen (ShowViewController). We are going to set up our PickerView &lt;code&gt;moodPicker&lt;/code&gt; now. Let&amp;rsquo;s define an array of Strings having three moods: &amp;ldquo;Happy,&amp;rdquo; &amp;ldquo;Meh,&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Sad.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// moods for moodPicker...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; moods: [String] = [&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Happy&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Meh&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Sad&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;] &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Also, let&amp;rsquo;s declare a variable that keeps the selected mode:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; selectedMood = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Happy&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now it&amp;rsquo;s time to set up the PickerView. To activate a PickerView, the class ShowViewController needs to adopt two &lt;a href="https://github.com/sakibnm/iOS/blob/main/10.-protocols"&gt;Protocols&lt;/a&gt;: UIPickerViewDelegate, and UIPickerViewDataSource. UIPickerViewDelegate is the protocol to enable user interactions with the PickerView, and UIPickerViewDataSource is the protocol to access data to display on PickerView.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>3.3.2. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: delegating to ViewController</title><link>/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.5.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-3-delegating-to-viewcontroller/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.5.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-3-delegating-to-viewcontroller/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="332-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-delegating-to-viewcontroller"&gt;3.3.2. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: delegating to ViewController&lt;a class="anchor" href="#332-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-delegating-to-viewcontroller"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s enable the action for &lt;code&gt;buttonSendMood&lt;/code&gt; in ShowViewController.swift file. So let&amp;rsquo;s update &lt;code&gt;viewDidLoad()&lt;/code&gt; function and add a new selector method &lt;code&gt;onSendButtonTapped()&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;{% code lineNumbers=&amp;ldquo;true&amp;rdquo; %}&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// setting up buttonSendMood...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;override&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;viewDidLoad&lt;/span&gt;() {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;super&lt;/span&gt;.viewDidLoad()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//setting the view background to white...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; view.backgroundColor = .white
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt; initializing the UI elements...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; setupLabelMessage()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; setupLabelMoodInstructions()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; setupMoodPicker()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; setupButtonSendMood()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt; setting up constraints...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; initConstraints()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt; add a delegate to on &lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//button send mode tapped...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; buttonSendMood.addTarget(&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;, action: &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;#selector&lt;/span&gt;(onSendMoodButtonTapped), &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt;: .touchUpInside)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt; on send button tapped...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;@objc&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;onSendMoodButtonTapped&lt;/span&gt;(){
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;{% endcode %}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>3.3.3. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIImageView</title><link>/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.6.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-4-uiimageview/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/03-introduction-to-uikit/multi-screen-apps/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.6.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-4-uiimageview/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="333-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uiimageview"&gt;3.3.3. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIImageView&lt;a class="anchor" href="#333-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uiimageview"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id="importing-images-into-the-project"&gt;Importing images into the project&lt;a class="anchor" href="#importing-images-into-the-project"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s start working with ImageViews. We need three images for moods: happy, meh, and sad. We will be using the following images in three different sizes: 1x, 2x, and 3x.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="/gitbook-assets/happy%20%281%29.png" alt="" /&gt; &lt;img src="/gitbook-assets/meh%20%281%29.png" alt="" /&gt; &lt;img src="/gitbook-assets/sad%20%281%29.png" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Download the images from here:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;{% file src=&amp;quot;/gitbook-assets/images (1).zip&amp;quot; %}&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you extract the files, you will see something like the following:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>